    description: "Version 0.2"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/NeoCortex0815/knowing-is-not-committing"
abstract: >-
  Independent replication and extension of MIT CSAIL's Sparks of Weight-Space
  Programming on Qwen3.5-0.8B. We rebuild the loop-reversal edit, add
  conditioned closing pushes and write a truth-gated reflex into 16 MLP
  neurons. A series of pre-registered tests asks how the model finds,
  recognises and commits to answers. Version 0.4 corrects a grading error of
  versions 0.2 and 0.3; five pre-registered verdicts change. Version 0.3
  reported N30, the test pre-registered publicly in v0.2: with corrected
  grading, a council of three answer-mode runs with our own thinking run as
  fallback solves 77 of 150 never-used MATH training problems, against 69 for
  answer mode alone and 67 for MIT's edit with thinking. It also reported N31: at the values the model writes while
  reasoning, its own tendency to stop does not track whether the value is
  correct (AUC 0.51), while a frozen linear probe does (0.68). Not
  peer-reviewed.
